Derived and corrected variant of automataIA/1brc-rs, binary v16_flat_table.

Upstream: https://github.com/automataIA/1brc-rs, commit
ab88b1bc2d14110a20191bc19803c5d5916382b8. The original is unchanged; this patch
applies to a copy of it.

License: MIT. The original notice is kept unchanged in LICENSE and applies to
this patch:
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 carcall. Permission is hereby granted,
    free of charge, ... (full text in LICENSE). THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED
    "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.

The patch fixes only the three ways the original breaks the official 1BRC
rules, minimally, and adds no speed:

  (A) It reads 8 bytes from every temperature start, also from the last row's
      at the end of the mmap: an unpadded file (the rules' input) panics
      "range end index 8 out of range" (lib.rs:127). The authors' generator
      pads the file with 8 NUL bytes; the rules' files are not padded.
  (B) Names are kept in [u8; 32] keys: a name longer than 32 bytes panics
      (hash.rs:164). The rules allow 100 bytes.
  (C) The table has 4096 slots, no growth and no fullness check: more than
      4096 stations make `locate` probe forever. The rules allow 10 000.

Hunks, in file order:

  src/bin/v16_flat_table.rs
    @@ -45 (A): `process_chunk` runs the original row loop (moved unchanged
        into `process_rows`) up to the first row that starts within 109 bytes
        of the end of the mapping (109 = 100-byte name + ';' + the 8-byte
        read from the temperature start); the rows after it
        are parsed from a copy padded with 8 zero bytes, as beowolx/fast_1brc
        does. Only the last chunk ever has such rows; the hot loop is the
        original's, with `stop` instead of `end` as its loop bound.
    @@ -57 (A): the moved loop returns where it stopped.

  src/hash.rs
    @@ -120 (C): FLAT_SLOTS 4096 -> 16 384 (load <= 0.61 at 10 000 stations,
        the primary table size beowolx uses). Each per-thread table grows from
        ~266 KB to ~1.4 MB of address space (+384 KB for `long`, untouched
        except at the slots of long names).
    @@ -129 (B): new field `long: Vec<Vec<u8>>`, the full name of a slot whose
        name is longer than 32 bytes; empty and unallocated otherwise.
    @@ -152 (B): `long` initialised with empty vectors.
    @@ -159 (B): the inline key takes the first min(len, 32) bytes instead of
        asserting len <= 32.
    @@ -171 (B): on insert a long name is also stored whole; on a hit (same
        stored 64-bit hash, same length, same first 32 bytes) a long name must
        also match in bytes 32.. . Names of <= 32 bytes take one extra
        predictable compare (`name.len() <= 32`) on a hit.
    @@ -190 (B): `merge_from` reads the whole name through `name(i)`.
    @@ -203 (B): `into_btree` reads the whole name through `name(i)`; new
        helper `name(i)`.

Not changed: `chunk_bounds` (lib.rs) ignores up to 16 bytes after the last
`\n`, so a final row without `\n` of at most 16 bytes is dropped silently
(a file ending in "Last;-5.3" without "\n" loses that row); a longer one is counted. The rules say line
endings are `\n`, so a valid file ends with one; not repaired. v17_prefetch
shares FlatTable and is not part of this variant.

